From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 28/29] superio/smsc/sch555x: Share the EC mailbox, report fans

The OptiPlex 9020 and the sklkbl desktops carry identical copies of the
SCH5555 EC mailbox code. Move it into the Super I/O driver as
sch555x_mbox_read() and sch555x_mbox_write().

Add what's needed to watch the fans of the EC's hardware monitor, whose
registers follow the SCH5627 (Linux sch5627: count = 5400540 / RPM,
0xffff when stopped):

- sch555x_fan_failure(): whether a monitored fan is stopped or below
  its minimum speed, giving a fan one second to spin up. The firmware
  programs the minimum of each fan it wants monitored; the others keep
  the reset value 0xffff, so no board needs to list its fans.
- acpi/fan.asl: an ACPI fan device (PNP0C0B) for each monitored fan, so
  the OS can read the speed through _FST. The EC keeps controlling the
  fans, so each has one performance state the OS can't change. The full
  ACPI 4.0 set (_FIF, _FPS, _FSL, _FST) is there because Linux before
  6.15 only reports the speed with all four.

Include it in both boards' DSDTs. The EC mailbox isn't used from SMM, so
the AML method owns it while the OS runs.

